cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Angelica in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Angelica"
abstract: >
  Angelica is an open-source platform for steady, incompressible pipe network
  simulation. It computes nodal pressures, flow rates, and (in non-isothermal
  mode) temperatures in networks of pipes, fittings, pumps, and inline heat
  sources. The hydraulic solver uses a pressure-correction algorithm (modified
  SIMPLE) with Colebrook-White, Hazen-Williams, or Poiseuille closures. The
  non-isothermal extension wraps the hydraulic solver in an outer temperature
  loop, solving the energy equation with NTU-based heat loss and Moukalled
  source-term linearisation. A graphical network editor is included.
authors:
